  "limits": [
    "Six samples per lane do not characterize tail latency.",
    "Gateway wall time can include background work. Browser minus Gateway wall is arithmetic residual, not measured transport latency.",
    "Root wait is nested within admission bind. Router preparation and A execution overlap. Do not sum those spans.",
    "Staging tails include unrelated traffic. This record joins Gateway POST by CF-Ray and Router spans by trace ID.",
    "The first sample verifier initially lacked arms.json. Its successful raw registration was preserved, metadata was supplied, and its independent proof then passed. No registration was rerun or excluded.",
    "Staging had ten additional respond POSTs while production had none. Their effect on backend warmth is not isolated.",
    "Authentication-stage medians were 704.25 ms staging and 429.4 ms production. Preparation continues during authentication, so even post-passkey timings depend on this duration.",
    "First-of-run does not by itself prove a cold Worker or a completely idle backend. No general no-regression conclusion follows from these small, differently loaded populations."
  ],
